From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: round hybrid attention block to a multiple of 64

For hybrid GDN+attention models the attention KV block is aligned up to
the mamba page (e.g. 1056). When VLLM_MUSA_ATTN_BLOCK64=1, round it up to
a multiple of 64 so the paged KV can be viewed as page_size=64 at the mate
FMHA call and take the TME fast path. Off by default (no behaviour change).
---
 vllm/platforms/interface.py | 9 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/platforms/interface.py b/vllm/platforms/interface.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/vllm/platforms/interface.py
+++ b/vllm/platforms/interface.py
@@ -768,6 +768,16 @@
                 kernel_block_alignment_size * attn_page_size_1_token,
             )

+        import os as _os
+
+        if (
+            _os.environ.get("VLLM_MUSA_ATTN_BLOCK64", "0") == "1"
+            and attn_block_size % 64 != 0
+        ):
+            # MUSA: round the hybrid attention block up to a multiple of 64 so
+            # the paged KV can be viewed as page_size=64 at the mate FMHA call
+            # (TME fast path). mamba padding is recomputed below from this block.
+            attn_block_size = ((attn_block_size + 63) // 64) * 64
         if cache_config.block_size < attn_block_size:
             cache_config.block_size = attn_block_size
             logger.info(
